  470: # REQ-001's six edge functions. One block each, and `verify_jwt` is STATED rather than inherited: a
  471: # default that changed underneath us would silently open a public path. Writing it down means a
  472: # change to the default shows up as a diff rather than as a behaviour nobody chose.
  473: #
  474: # FIVE OF THE SIX OPERATE FOR AN ALREADY-AUTHENTICATED CALLER. This comment used to say all of them
  475: # did, which was true of the first three and is not true any more: `public-project-page` is the
  476: # repository's FIRST public function and the correction lands in the same change that adds it.
  477: #
  478: # WHY EXACTLY ONE IS PUBLIC. AT-001.22 says a project's public page remains visible while its
  479: # non-public data is denied, and AT-001.24 says a logged-out visitor renders public surfaces only. A
  480: # surface that refused everybody would satisfy the denial half of both criteria and break the other
  481: # half. Keeping the public answer in its OWN function, rather than as a branch inside
  482: # `project-workspace`, is what stops it contaminating AT-001.21's no-existence-oracle test: the two
  483: # authenticated read surfaces have one refusal and no public branch to fall through to.
  484: [functions.complete-signup]
  485: verify_jwt = true
  486: 
  487: [functions.create-organization]
  488: verify_jwt = true
  489: 
  490: [functions.update-organization]
  491: verify_jwt = true
  492: 
  493: [functions.organization-dashboard]
  494: verify_jwt = true
  495: 
  496: [functions.project-workspace]
  497: verify_jwt = true
  498: 
  499: # THE ONE PUBLIC FUNCTION. See the paragraph above; the value is `false` on purpose and a change to
  500: # `true` would break AT-001.22's second clause.
  501: [functions.public-project-page]
  502: verify_jwt = false
